{"sourceSha256": "6822ec27e722120a6de3714c541f92e037a4a8e350cc1cb393e01d7ffcbd468e", "text": "Ticket Id: 16460\n\n01/06/2014\n\nDr Charles White\nThyroid Specialist\nBayview Private Hospital\n81 Canyon Road\nBayview\n\nDear Dr White,\n\nRe: Ms Lola Duval,    aged 24 years old\n\nI am writing this letter to refer you Ms Duval, a 24-year-old engineering student, who complains of\nunexpected weight loss in the last two months. Your earliest review would be highly appreciated.\n\nOn 31/05/2014, Ms Duval attended my surgery complaining of tremors, episodic palpitations, sweating,\nheat intolerance in the last two – months as well as fatigue in the last month. Moreover, she was anxious\nand concerned about her weight lost. Upon examination, her weight was 55 kg and she had slightly              Commented [JG1]: loss\nenlarged thyroid gland without tenderness. In addition, her eyes had lid lag associated with some             Commented [JG2]: a\nexophthalmos. Thus, some investigations were ordered. Please note, she has a medical history of anxiety\nand insomnia for which she has been taking sleeping pills occasionally.\n\nToday, Ms Duval test results came in showing sinus tachycardia in her ECG and her thyroid function test\nshowed that TSH level is less than 0.05 as well as elevation in free T3 by 15 pmol/L and free T4 by 40        Commented [JG3]: was\npmol/L. Therefore, a thyroid scan and thyroid auto-antibody tests were ordered.\n\nIn light of the above, my provisional diagnosis is hyperthyroidism. I would be grateful if you could assess\nand review her condition as soon as possible as the patient is anxious. If you have any queries, please do\nnot hesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nDoctor\n                                     Report\n Word length                  217\n Comments                     Well done! The grammar, sentence structure and\n                              word choices are accurate, and the information is\n                              cl